-- title:
--   Exceptional valuation ring recovered from the affine chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. For a field $K$, a place `Place K F` of a $K$-extension $F$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, whose ideals are principal; `P.ord f` is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb Z^{m0}$-valued adic valuation at $f$, and `P.evalAt f` is the preimage in $K$ (under the inverse of $K \to$ residue field of $P$) of the residue class of $f$ when $f$ lies in the valuation ring, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   **Setting.** A prime $q$ with $q = 2$ is fixed, together with a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`A.LiesOverPrime q`), with residue field $\kappa :=$ `ResidueField A`; a finite set $W$ of places of $F_\kappa :=$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the intermediate field of $\kappa \subseteq \kappa((t))$ generated by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) over $\kappa$, required by `hW` to consist exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. of those $w$ which are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M' w`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`; and a chosen element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   Write $\bar F_{M'} :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the $\mathbb Q$-subfield of $\mathbb Q((t))$ generated by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid M'$), and $\bar F :=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the analogous base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the unit-group reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion $\bar F_{M'} \le \bar F$, used for the comparison map `IntermediateField.inclusion hle`.
--
--   **Constant reduction.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC κ M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\bar F_{M'}$ meeting the constants exactly in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism `R₀.residue : R₀.integers →+* F_κ` with kernel the maximal ideal and agreeing on constants with the residue map of $A$, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places which preserves degrees and is compatible with divisors of non-vanishing residue, and the scaling clause that every non-zero element of $\bar F_{M'}$ has a constant multiple in `R₀.integers` with non-zero residue (these structure fields are summarised here). The hypothesis `hR₀` states: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that image lies in `R₀.integers`, and its $R_0$-residue, viewed inside $\kappa((t))$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Small constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr` and `hunif` state that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, and `hκ` states that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. An index $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the $q$-th primitive roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is given. Further, $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements of $K_b$ lying in $A$ (`hAb`), and $\varpi_b \in A_b$ a non-zero generator of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **The exceptional valuation ring.** $\mathcal O'$ is a valuation subring of $\bar F$ subject to three clauses. (A) `hO'_A`: for $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ in $\bar F$ lies in $\mathcal O'$ if and only if $x \in A$. (OVER) `hO'_over`: for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $P$ of $\bar F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the base-changed $j$-series `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $\mathcal O'$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $\mathcal O'$ and in its maximal ideal. (FIX) `hO'_fix`: for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the comap of $\mathcal O'$ along the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` of $\bar F$ is $\mathcal O'$ itself (here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the automorphism of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ singled out by the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar`, and the identity if none exists).
--
--   **Assertion.** Equip $\bar F$ with the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \bar F$ stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that (i) for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, (ii) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, (iii) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal, and (iv) ($W_0$ lies over $s$) for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, has non-negative order at every place of $\bar F_{M'}$ where the base-changed $j$-series does, and has $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ in $\bar F$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $g$ and of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal; for every subring $B$ of $\bar F$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure such that (M1) the structure map $A_b \to B$ is induced by $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, (M2) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, (M3) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element, (M4) an element $f$ of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f\cdot h = g$ in $\bar F$ for some $g, h \in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$, (M5) $B$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and (E1) for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every `IsDomain` structure on [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[x,y]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field, inside the fraction field of the coordinate ring, of the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `hFunctionFieldAction` attached to the pairs $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta' \in C_s$) such that $\#C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (which, $q$ being $2$, is $12$ or $1$ according as $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$ vanishes or not, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`), $\ker \rho$ is generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, $\rho$ agrees on $A_b$ with the reduction $A \to \kappa$ followed by $\kappa \to$ `quotField`, every element of `quotField` is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $\rho(h) \ne 0$ and $g,h \in B$, an element of `quotField` lies in the range of $\rho$ exactly when it lies, inside the Drinfeld function field, in the image of the coordinate ring, and $\rho$ is equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` in $B$, the image under $\rho$ of that translate is obtained from $\rho(f)$ by `hFunctionFieldAction` at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$; and finally for every finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ whose cardinality is $q+1$ and which satisfies (N-EQV) for each $\zeta$, each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and each $O \in$ `nodes` there is $O_1 \in$ `nodes` with $f \in O \iff \mathrm{levelAutBar}\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in O_1$ for all $f \in F_0$ whose translate again lies in $F_0$, (N-TRANS) for each $\zeta$ and each ordered pair $O, O_1 \in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ realising the same equivalence, (N-SEP) for distinct $O, O_1 \in$ `nodes` there is an element of $F_0$ belonging to both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O_1$, and (COVER) for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ satisfying the conditions (i) and (iv) above with $V$ in place of $W_0$, either every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or there is $O \in$ `nodes` with $O$ contained in $V$ and every non-unit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$ —
--
--   then, for every $f \in F_0$, $f$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $\mathcal O'$.
--
--   Thus the conclusion is the single equivalence identifying $W_0$ with the trace of $\mathcal O'$ on $F_0$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the identification of the exceptional valuation ring above a supersingular point with the one prescribed by an affine Drinfeld chart in the semistable model of the full-level modular curve. It is used in the construction of node charts and of the specialisation of the Drinfeld coordinate ring, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local_of_eq_two_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
